<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Walker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1824–1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Walker was an American filibuster from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>. In 1853 he raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baja-california">Baja California</a> and proclaimed a short-lived Republic of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Invited into Nicaragua's civil war by the liberals of León, he made himself president in 1856 and restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, until a Central American coalition led by Costa Rica drove him out in 1857. He was executed in Honduras in 1860.</p></div>
